{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00841",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 17.39,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "Mr Calder? I'm Heather, the nurse. I'll put your drops in for the eye test in a moment, but first, a couple of questions for the doctor's record. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.81,
      "end_seconds": 25.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Certainly. I'd rather like to get the details right, so do ask. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.58,
      "end_seconds": 35.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Good morning, Mr Calder. I understand light has become uncomfortable since you were ill."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.24,
      "end_seconds": 57.49,
      "duration_seconds": 20.25,
      "text": "Yes. Three weeks ago I had a viral illness, a fever, aches, a streaming cold. Since then, bright light, sunlight, even the strip lights in the supermarket, hurts my eyes. I squint, and my eyes water."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.16,
      "end_seconds": 61.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Is it both eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.8,
      "end_seconds": 74.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Both, equally. There's no redness, and no pain as such, only a discomfort in bright light, like a glare."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.4,
      "end_seconds": 81.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Any change in your vision? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.24,
      "end_seconds": 84.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "None whatsoever. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 85.3,
      "end_seconds": 91.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Any allergies, Mr Calder? We need it for the drops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.84,
      "end_seconds": 112.66,
      "duration_seconds": 18.82,
      "text": "Well, that's an interesting one. I think I may have had a reaction to some eye drops years ago, but I can't tell you which drops, or what the reaction was. I've never been sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.04,
      "end_seconds": 123.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "I'll note that as a possible reaction, not confirmed, substance and reaction unknown. Any medicines you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.19,
      "end_seconds": 130.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Just one, lansoprazole, 15 mg, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.47,
      "end_seconds": 137.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Any family history of eye problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 144.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "My mother had glaucoma, and my uncle had macular degeneration."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 145.29,
      "end_seconds": 156.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "Doctor, since the allergy is uncertain, shall I use the plain dilating drops without the preservative, as we normally do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 163.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Please do, Heather, and watch him for ten minutes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 189.91,
      "end_seconds": 191.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.71,
      "end_seconds": 199.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Now, with the drops in, I'll examine you in a while. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.19,
      "end_seconds": 203.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 204.22,
      "end_seconds": 210.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "His eyes have dilated nicely, doctor, and there's no reaction. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.57,
      "end_seconds": 237.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Thank you. Mr Calder, chin on the rest, look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.1,
      "end_seconds": 252.85,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "The front of both eyes is clear, with no inflammation, no redness, the pressure's normal, and the back of the eye looks healthy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.74,
      "end_seconds": 258.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Is that good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.17,
      "end_seconds": 275.58,
      "duration_seconds": 14.41,
      "text": "It is. Light sensitivity after a viral illness, with a normal examination, is common, and it usually settles over a few weeks. I'd say this is post-viral light sensitivity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.15,
      "end_seconds": 281.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "How long will it last? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.41,
      "end_seconds": 289.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Weeks, occasionally a couple of months. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.42,
      "end_seconds": 296.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Is there anything I should do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.65,
      "end_seconds": 309.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Wear good sunglasses outdoors, and a brimmed hat, and don't stay in a dark room, as that can make the eyes more sensitive."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.37,
      "end_seconds": 317.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "I'd been staying in rather a dim room. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.49,
      "end_seconds": 325.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Gradual exposure to normal light is better. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.64,
      "end_seconds": 328.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Understood. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.73,
      "end_seconds": 342.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.67,
      "text": "If your vision changes, you get eye pain, redness, or a severe headache, or it's still bothering you in six weeks, come back to see me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.82,
      "end_seconds": 348.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, both. ~"
    }
  ]
}
